# stigmergy — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. `.env` is gitignored and never enters a Docker build
# context. Nothing here is required to run the test suite: `make test` is keyless by construction
# (an autouse fixture forces the fake LLM backend repo-wide, even against a populated `.env`), and
# `make db-up` brings up the local Postgres and MinIO with the defaults already baked in.
#
# You only need a section once you run the thing it configures.

# ── the knowledge repository ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This platform stores no pages. It reads and writes a separate git repository — the "knowledge
# repo" — whose layout is described in docs/reference/knowledge-repo.md. Point this at your own
# checkout.
STIGMERGY_REPO=../stigmergy-brain

# ── the derived index (required for anything that searches) ─────────────────────────────────────
# `make db-up` serves exactly this DSN. Override for a hosted Postgres.
STIGMERGY_INDEX_DSN=postgresql://stigmergy:stigmergy@localhost:54321/stigmergy
# The suites truncate their tables at fixture setup, so they use a SEPARATE database. Setting this
# is also the "CI mode" signal: with it set, an unreachable database FAILS the run instead of
# skipping every Postgres suite.
STIGMERGY_TEST_DSN=postgresql://stigmergy:stigmergy@localhost:54321/stigmergy_test

# ── models ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend selection is per-seam so an offline double can stand in for any of them.
# CLEAN_LLM=fake gives a deterministic offline backend; the suite forces it regardless.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# CLEAN_LLM=openai
# CLEAN_MODEL=
# ANSWER_LLM=openai
# ANSWER_MODEL=
# VISION_MODEL=
# STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_MODEL=
# STIGMERGY_GARDENER_MODEL=

# ── the evidence plane (S3-compatible: MinIO locally, any S3 in production) ──────────────────────
# `make db-up` starts MinIO; these defaults match it.
STIGMERGY_EVIDENCE_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
STIGMERGY_EVIDENCE_BUCKET=stigmergy-evidence
STIGMERGY_EVIDENCE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
STIGMERGY_EVIDENCE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin

# ── the librarian worker (writes to the knowledge repo through a GitHub App) ─────────────────────
# Create the App with Contents: read and write on your knowledge repo only. See
# docs/reference/librarian.md for the full walkthrough.
STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_APP_ID=
STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_INSTALLATION_ID=
STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=
STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_REPO_URL=
# STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_BACKEND=double     # `double` runs the offline agent — no API key needed
# STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_BRANCH=main
# STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_TIMEOUT_S=
# STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_MAX_TURNS=
# STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=

# ── the HTTP transport ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A JSON map of sha256(token) -> identity. Generate a token hash with `stigmergy-issue-token`.
# STIGMERGY_TOKEN_STORE={"<sha256hex>": "steward@example.com"}
# STIGMERGY_TOKEN_STORE_FILE=
# STIGMERGY_PUBLIC_HOST=          # bare hostname, no scheme
# STIGMERGY_IDENTITY=             # stdio only: which identity to serve as
# The baked stewards map a process with NO knowledge-repo checkout resolves review authority from.
# The deployed app/slack groups get it as `--stewards /app/stewards.json` (fly.toml), not from
# here; set it locally only to exercise that path. Where a checkout exists the repo read wins.
# STIGMERGY_STEWARDS_PATH=

# ── the Slack transport (Socket Mode — no inbound port) ─────────────────────────────────────────
SLACK_APP_TOKEN=
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
SLACK_TEAM_ID=
# Named in the bot's own copy when a user needs a human ("ask <name> to add you").
# Defaults to "your steward".
# STIGMERGY_STEWARD_NAME=

# ── the incremental index webhook ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STIGMERGY_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# STIGMERGY_GITHUB_REPO=<owner>/stigmergy-brain
# STIGMERGY_GITHUB_BRANCH=main

# ── the admin console (optional — unset means the console does not exist) ────────────────────────
# Hash from `stigmergy-admin-token`. Without it every /admin route is inert.
# STIGMERGY_ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH=
# STIGMERGY_ADMIN_GITHUB_TOKEN=   # fine-grained PAT, Actions read+write, this repo only
# STIGMERGY_ADMIN_GITHUB_REPO=<owner>/<repo>
# STIGMERGY_DIGEST_CHANNEL_ID=

# ── the gardener's thresholds (all optional, all have defaults) ──────────────────────────────────
# STIGMERGY_GARDENER_AGING_SEED_DAYS=30
# STIGMERGY_GARDENER_CONCENTRATION_WINDOW=30
# STIGMERGY_GARDENER_CONCENTRATION_SHARE=0.6
# STIGMERGY_GARDENER_COMPANY_WINDOW=20
# STIGMERGY_GARDENER_COMPANY_SHARE=0.3
# STIGMERGY_GARDENER_SWEEP_SAMPLE=
# STIGMERGY_DIGEST_WINDOW_DAYS=

# ── external binaries the code shells out to ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are looked up on PATH by default; set these only if yours live elsewhere.
# STIGMERGY_GITLEAKS_BIN=gitleaks     # the secrets gate REFUSES to file without a working scanner
# STIGMERGY_DRIVE_GOG_BIN=

# ── the operator drop CLIs (`stigmergy-meeting drop`, `stigmergy-drive drop`) ───────────────────────
# Who a drop is attributed to when `--submitted-by` is not passed.
# STIGMERGY_MEETING_OPERATOR_EMAIL=

# ── object-store smoke check (scripts/r2_smoke.py, `make r2-smoke`) ─────────────────────────────
# These four belong to the smoke check ALONE. Nothing else reads them: the server, the worker and
# the operator drop CLIs all read the STIGMERGY_EVIDENCE_* group above. The namespaces stay separate
# on purpose — "which bucket does the running server write to" must be answerable without knowing
# which script last touched the environment.
#
# The consequence to know, because it cost a lost capture: `set -a; source .env` with only these
# set LOOKS like it configured the evidence plane and does not, so a drop against a remote
# deployment would upload the bytes to whatever local MinIO this file's own STIGMERGY_EVIDENCE_ENDPOINT
# names while queueing the row remotely.
# To point an operator CLI at a deployment, export the STIGMERGY_EVIDENCE_* group with these values.
# The drop CLIs refuse that exact combination (remote queue + loopback store) before anything
# is fetched, uploaded or queued, rather than failing eight seconds later inside the worker.
# R2_ENDPOINT_URL=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=

# ── deploying to Fly staging (`make deploy-staging`) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tracked fly.toml ships with CHANGEME placeholders on purpose: a deployment's real
# coordinates never live in this repo. flyctl prefers $FLY_APP over fly.toml's `app`, and the two
# machine-facing values (STIGMERGY_PUBLIC_HOST, STIGMERGY_LIBRARIAN_REPO_URL) are Fly SECRETS set once
# on the app — secrets take precedence over the `[env]` placeholders, so the pristine template
# deploys as-is. The Makefile exports this whole file into every target, so with FLY_APP here a
# deploy is exactly `make deploy-staging`, nothing else.
# FLY_APP=<your-fly-app>
# The staging index DSN, for `make rebuild-staging` — deliberately NOT STIGMERGY_INDEX_DSN, so a
# local `make test` or `make index-rebuild` can never point at staging by accident.
# STAGING_DSN=
